{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607051800-net-babiniku-vrm-vtuber-design"
  :title "ADR-2607051800: net-babiniku -- a new gftdcojp product, AI VTuber/VRM companion
          chat, distinct from network-isekai but sharing the kami engine"
  :status "proposed"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "net-babiniku-vrm-vtuber"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-05"
  :authoritative_for
  ["gftdcojp/net-babiniku is a NEW, separate repo from gftdcojp/network-isekai -- both
    render VRM avatars via the same kotoba-lang/kami-engine substrate, but through
    different integration layers (Svelte + @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk for net-babiniku vs
    hand-rolled ClojureScript/reagent glue for network-isekai) and for different audiences
    (private single-purpose AI-companion product vs open public forkable game platform)"
   "net-babiniku's product shape is modeled on isekaizero.ai (interactive AI stories,
    choices-matter roleplay chat, per-character voice) but replaces its 2D visual-novel
    character portraits with a live-rendered 3D VRM avatar (VTuber presentation), via
    kami-engine-sdk's VrmViewer/createVrmEngine"
   "net-babiniku reuses kami-engine-sdk's `webvr` headless choice-scenario runner
    (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph, pluggable onScene renderer) --
    originally built for cyber-drill's incident-response drills -- repurposed to
    conversational roleplay content, supplying VrmViewer as the onScene renderer instead
    of cyber-drill's vendor-private three.js scene"
   "AI-persona content is containment + governor per the existing Actors doctrine: the
    LLM-persona node proposes {dialogue, emotion, motion-cue} only; a separate
    ContentGovernor filters before anything renders to the VRM avatar or is spoken via
    TTS; every commit/hold is appended to an audit ledger"
   "net-babiniku's data model is private/per-user (chat sessions, personas, avatar
    customization), NOT network-isekai's public content-addressed everything-forkable EDN
    model -- kotoba-style content-addressing may still be used internally for asset
    caching only"]
  :related
  ["90-docs/adr/2607032400-network-isekai-primary-consolidation.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607041430-network-isekai-reagent-spa-consolidation.md"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "user direction 2026-07-05: design gftdcojp/net-babiniku, separate from
           gftdcojp/network-isekai, sharing the same kami engine, shaped as a VRM/VTuber
           app in the spirit of isekaizero.ai"
  :investigated
  ["isekaizero.ai (ISEKAI ZERO, ARX MEDIA SDN BHD): interactive AI story/roleplay mobile
    app, #1 Games/#2 Entertainment App Store (2026-05), chat with LLM characters +
    choices-matter narrative + experimental Visual Novel Mode (2D background/character
    images with expression/pose swaps + per-character TTS), multi-LLM backend
    (Deepseek 3.2 default, switchable Gemini/Grok), Mana(free)/Arcane(paid) dual currency"
   "network-isekai is an open 'CodePen for games' platform: games + VRM :dance stages
    (kami.dance/kami-live vocabulary, isekai.stage.cljc + isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc hand-rolled
    against kami-web wasm directly) + asset hub, everything public/forkable EDN in Datomic
    via kotoba -- VRM is one mode among several, not the product's identity, and the
    public/forkable data model is wrong for private AI-companion chat sessions"
   "kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk (@etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk, Svelte 5, three.js-free per
    ADR-2605264300) already packages VrmViewer/createVrmEngine (live VRM avatar via
    Rust+wgpu WASM KamiWasmExports, no three.js) + headless morph/bone/motion/voice/
    emotion builders + `./webvr` (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph,
    pluggable onScene renderer) -- built after network-isekai's own vrm-bridge glue, for
    exactly this kind of app"
   "no existing product combines webvr's choice engine with VrmViewer as the onScene
    renderer; cyber-drill (the only current webvr consumer) supplies its own vendor-private
    three.js renderer for incident-response drills, an unrelated domain"
   "gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai checked and is unrelated -- a Minecraft-voxel-sandbox x
    creature-collection game (isekai.gftd.ai) sharing kami-engine's WebGPU renderer and the
    'isekai' name only coincidentally"]
  :risk "AI-companion/roleplay chat is a known content-moderation surface; 'babiniku'
         (バ美肉, embodying a VRM/VTuber persona) framing raises the stakes of getting the
         containment/governor boundary right from the start, not as a retrofit."}

 :decision
 {:repo {:org "gftdcojp" :visibility :private
         :rationale "human-centric/business scope per repos.edn :orgs; gftdcojp default
                     visibility is private per repos.edn :orgs :visibility (ADR-2607021330)"
         :registration "plain-git child repo, manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects ->
                        manifest/west.yml, --entry net-babiniku minimal-diff generation"}
  :frontend
  {:stack "Svelte 5 via @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk (VrmViewer/createVrmEngine), NOT
           network-isekai's ClojureScript/reagent"
   :rationale "the SDK already packages the live-avatar render surface (wgpu/WASM,
               three.js-free); network-isekai's isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc/isekai.stage.cljc
               predate the SDK and hand-roll the same glue directly against kami-web wasm
               -- no reason to redo that work in CLJS for a second app"}
  :turn_engine
  {:what "kami-engine-sdk's `webvr` headless choice-scenario runner
          (createIncidentVrEngine, langgraph/Pregel StateGraph), repurposed from
          incident-response drill content to conversational-roleplay content"
   :renderer "VrmViewer supplied as the onScene callback -- net-babiniku is webvr's
              SECOND consumer (after cyber-drill) and FIRST VrmViewer-as-onScene consumer,
              validating the headless-engine/pluggable-renderer split across two
              unrelated domains"}
  :expression_motion
  {:model "each LLM turn emits {dialogue emotion motion-cue}; emotion drives the SDK's
           morph builder (facial blend-shape targets), motion-cue drives the bone/motion
           builder (idle/gesture pose) -- data-driven render state, same philosophy as
           kami.dance's pose-from-EDN but keyed to conversation turns instead of a beat
           grid"}
  :voice
  {:what "SDK's voice builder drives per-character TTS, matching isekaizero.ai's
          per-character-voice Visual Novel Mode but spoken through a live avatar"
   :backend "net-babiniku stands up its OWN backend (LLM chat completion + TTS) --
             independent deploy from network-isekai's backend/ (Modal GPU: TRELLIS/
             image/TTS/music); where the same Modal-GPU-TTS pattern applies, copy-adapt
             rather than cross-repo depend, matching isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc's own
             precedent for character-creator's gpu-adapter"}
  :ai_persona_containment
  {:pattern "Actors doctrine (CLAUDE.md Actors section; precedent isekai.moderation.cljc):
             LLM-persona node proposes {dialogue emotion motion-cue} only; a separate
             ContentGovernor filters before anything renders to the VRM avatar or is
             spoken via TTS; every commit/hold appended to an audit ledger"
   :non_negotiable true}
  :data_model
  {:what "private, per-user chat sessions / personas / avatar customization -- NOT
          network-isekai's public content-addressed everything-forkable EDN model"
   :kotoba_use "content-addressing may still be used internally for asset caching
                (avatar/voice asset dedup) only -- no public asset hub, no fork-by-URL"}}

 :consequences
 {:shared_engine_different_layers "net-babiniku and network-isekai both render VRM via the
                                    same kotoba-lang/kami-engine substrate, through
                                    different integration layers fit to each app's own
                                    stack/audience"
  :sdk_validation "validates kami-engine-sdk's webvr + pluggable-onScene design as reusable
                   across two unrelated domains (incident-response drills, AI-companion
                   roleplay)"
  :new_backend_needed "standalone backend (LLM chat + TTS + governor) and private data
                       store to build; nothing inherited automatically from
                       network-isekai's backend/"
  :scaffold_shape_followup "network-isekai-like scaffold (README + 90-docs/adr +
                            package.json, ADR-driven), not ai-gftd-isekai's dodaf
                            PROJECT.jsonld/OWNERS/nanoid shape -- net-babiniku is a
                            kami-engine app in network-isekai's lineage, not part of the
                            ai-gftd-*/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp product-registry line"
  :out_of_scope_followup "exact LLM provider(s), pricing/currency model, and detailed
                          moderation policy are product decisions out of scope for this
                          architecture ADR"}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "build it as a new mode/page inside network-isekai (like assets.html/
            generate.html today)"
   :rejected_because "different audience (private product vs open platform) and different
                       data model (private chat sessions vs public forkable EDN) --
                       architecturally wrong, not a styling difference; would also keep
                       the ClojureScript/re-frame stack instead of the SDK's native Svelte
                       packaging"}
  {:option "reimplement VRM rendering glue directly (network-isekai's own
            isekai.vrm-bridge.cljc + isekai.stage.cljc pattern) instead of depending on
            kami-engine-sdk"
   :rejected_because "the SDK already packages VrmViewer + morph/bone/voice/emotion
                       builders for exactly this; redoing it in CLJS+JS glue duplicates
                       real, already-built work for no benefit"}
  {:option "reuse cyber-drill's three.js scene renderer as the webvr onScene
            implementation"
   :rejected_because "cyber-drill's renderer is vendor-private and three.js-based; the SDK
                       is explicitly three.js-free (ADR-2605264300) and VrmViewer's native
                       wgpu path is the better-fit, on-brand renderer for a VTuber avatar
                       body"}]}
